<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Taillebourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">21–22 July <a href="/years/1242">1242</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintonge-war">Saintonge War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Taillebourg was fought on 21–22 July 1242 at the bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charente">Charente</a> at Taillebourg in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintonge">Saintonge</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> and his allies the Lusignans, and a further victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintes">Saintes</a> followed. The failure ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s attempt to recover Poitou and doomed the revolt of Raymond VII of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-taillebourg.jpg" alt="Battle of Taillebourg" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chroniques de Saint-Denis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis9_vs_Henri3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The French crown conquered Poitou between 1204 and 1224, when Louis VIII took La Rochelle, and Henry III's attempt to recover it failed at the <b>Battle of Taillebourg</b> in 1242.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Duchy of Aquitaine · Military</a></li></ul></section>
